Script	What it does	Skip if...
ingest.py	                OCR new PDFs → text	Never skip — has to run first, but it auto-skips already-processed files (remember the if os.path.exists(out_path) check), so it's cheap to re-run even with old + new resumes mixed together
check_extraction.py       	Sanity check for OCR failures	Optional, but good habit especially with new resumes you haven't seen the layout of yet
clean.py	                Tidies raw text	Re-run always — it's fast, just re-processes everything in data/extracted/
chunk.py	                Splits into bullets	Re-run always — also fast, reprocesses everything in data/cleaned/
dedupe_boilerplate.py	    Removes repeated headers	Re-run always — needed since new resumes add new content to chunks.json
embed_store.py	            Embeds + stores in Chroma	This is the one to watch — see below

